--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Google ML Kit — com.google.mlkit:text-recognition
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ML Kit is NOT open source. It is a proprietary Google SDK distributed under the
ML Kit Terms of Service, which impose obligations on the app that ships it.

This is the reason LICENSE carries a linking exception. Rekhon's own code is
AGPL, ML Kit cannot be, and shipping an APK containing both would otherwise be an
unresolvable conflict rather than a licensing choice. The exception permits the
link and weakens no AGPL obligation on Rekhon's own source.

The practical consequence for you: a build of this repository is not a wholly
free artefact even though its source is, and a fork inherits Google's terms as
well as ours. Used by the on-device receipt scanner (issue 3.8).

The coupling is one class — MlKitReceiptTextRecognizer, behind the
ReceiptTextRecognizer interface — and no domain model names an ML Kit type. A
fully free build substituting an open-source recogniser is a contained change and
needs no part of the exception.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Google Tink — com.google.crypto.tink:tink-android
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Apache License 2.0. Named separately because SEC-003 makes it the only sanctioned
cryptography in this project: no hand-rolled crypto, review-blocking.

